{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b950023707f01888", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# FastSpeech: Fast, Robust and Controllable Text to Speech\narXiv: 1905.09263\nAuthors: Yi Ren, Yangjun Ruan, Xu Tan, Tao Qin, Sheng Zhao, Zhou Zhao, Tie-Yan Liu\nYear: 2019 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A novel feed-forward network based on Transformer is proposed to generate mel-spectrograms in parallel for non-autoregressive text to speech.\n  2. A length regulator is introduced to up-sample phoneme sequences based on predicted durations, bridging the length mismatch between phoneme and mel-spectrogram sequences.\n  3. A phoneme duration predictor is designed and trained using attention alignments extracted from an autoregressive teacher model to ensure hard monotonous alignments.\n  4. The proposed FastSpeech model achieves massive inference speedups of 270x for mel-spectrogram generation and 38x for end-to-end speech synthesis compared to autoregressive Transformer TTS.\n  5. The model nearly eliminates robustness issues such as word skipping and repeating that commonly plague autoregressive TTS systems.\n  6. Voice speed and prosody can be smoothly and explicitly controlled by adjusting the phoneme durations through the length regulator.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/功能-蒸馏加速, TTS/功能-快速生成", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "857efdcf-76ac-4d71-a31d-bc3e11b792a8", "uuid": "2f20fc22-9aac-4457-a986-1d1b3899d76a", "timestamp": "2026-07-31T07:12:53.039Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# FastSpeech: Fast, Robust and Controllable Text to Speech\narXiv: 1905.09263\nAuthors: Yi Ren, Yangjun Ruan, Xu Tan, Tao Qin, Sheng Zhao, Zhou Zhao, Tie-Yan Liu\nYear: 2019 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A novel feed-forward network based on Transformer is proposed to generate mel-spectrograms in parallel for non-autoregressive text to speech.\n  2. A length regulator is introduced to up-sample phoneme sequences based on predicted durations, bridging the length mismatch between phoneme and mel-spectrogram sequences.\n  3. A phoneme duration predictor is designed and trained using attention alignments extracted from an autoregressive teacher model to ensure hard monotonous alignments.\n  4. The proposed FastSpeech model achieves massive inference speedups of 270x for mel-spectrogram generation and 38x for end-to-end speech synthesis compared to autoregressive Transformer TTS.\n  5. The model nearly eliminates robustness issues such as word skipping and repeating that commonly plague autoregressive TTS systems.\n  6. Voice speed and prosody can be smoothly and explicitly controlled by adjusting the phoneme durations through the length regulator.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Transformer, TTS/功能-蒸馏加速, TTS/功能-快速生成", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
